WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:03.950 --> 00:05.720
Professor Platane, hello.

00:06.290 --> 00:07.360
Hey, Satoshi-kun.

00:07.940 --> 00:09.360
We'd like you to have a look at this guy.

00:10.730 --> 00:11.360
This little one!

00:12.240 --> 00:18.080
We found it the other day, but it's not listed in the Pokémon Zukan, so we thought you could tell us about it.

00:18.950 --> 00:28.810
Data broadcast giveaways for 3 weeks in a row! Today is the second giveaway, where you can receive an "alternate-colored Yveltal" in your video games!

00:20.210 --> 00:21.770
I've never seen it before either.

00:22.330 --> 00:24.120
If it's not listed in the Zukan,

00:24.690 --> 00:26.290
could that mean it's a new Pokémon species?

00:26.520 --> 00:28.320
What? You think so too?

00:28.650 --> 00:30.420
That would be amazing!

00:29.920 --> 00:39.820
During today's data broadcast, we'll announce a "universal serial code" with which you can receive an "alternate-colored Yveltal" in "Pocket Monsters X/Y/OR/AS"!
Push the d-button on your remote and participate in the broadcast!

00:30.690 --> 00:31.090
Yeah!

00:31.570 --> 00:33.930
Can you give it a spin?

00:34.220 --> 00:34.850
Okay!

00:37.280 --> 00:39.130
Not you. He means Squishy.

00:39.460 --> 00:40.970
Oh! Oops!

00:46.940 --> 00:48.480
I really have never seen it before.

00:49.120 --> 00:52.530
Its body is squishy. That's why its name is Squishy.

00:54.120 --> 00:55.440
I'll do some research of my own.

00:56.400 --> 00:57.940
If I come up with anything I'll call you.

00:58.420 --> 01:00.380
Satoshi-kun, you and the others continue observing it.

01:00.700 --> 01:01.860
Okay, we will.

01:02.560 --> 01:05.120
So cute! "Squishy", they said!

01:05.120 --> 01:07.820
It's the Pokémon those red guys were calling "Z", right?

01:07.820 --> 01:11.210
It's such a significant Pokémon that they even told Professor Platane about it!

01:11.460 --> 01:16.560
If it's a new species, doesn't that mean we can name it if we get it?

01:16.810 --> 01:18.010
Like "Musashi Beauty" or something.

01:18.010 --> 01:19.610
"Nyarth Special"!

01:19.610 --> 01:21.410
"Cool Kojiro" sounds nice, too.

01:22.860 --> 01:24.080
Let the operation begin!

01:24.080 --> 01:24.700
Roger!

01:37.250 --> 01:38.910
Squishy, do you like it in here?

01:43.500 --> 01:44.660
What now...?

01:45.200 --> 01:47.290
That's right! Leave this to me!

01:47.570 --> 01:49.040
I'll make you something special!

01:49.530 --> 01:50.620
Really? You'll do that for me?

01:50.970 --> 01:52.410
All right!

01:56.370 --> 02:02.050
Hot-blooded Hariborg!
Squishy is Being Targeted!!

02:02.520 --> 02:10.410
Satoshi and his friends were continuing their journey to the Eisetsu Gym in order to get the eighth Gym badge needed to participate in the Kalos League.

02:39.610 --> 02:41.800
It really likes sunbathing.

02:47.370 --> 02:51.400
It might be turning the sunlight into energy for itself.

02:51.870 --> 02:52.830
Come to think of it...

02:58.990 --> 03:01.450
The sunlight is its substitute for food, right?

03:01.900 --> 03:02.710
Wow...

03:06.090 --> 03:09.710
The sun is its food? It can live without eating anything?

03:10.190 --> 03:11.870
This is getting more and more interesting.

03:12.310 --> 03:17.190
If we conduct research on it, we might be able to live without eating too.

03:17.480 --> 03:19.640
Zero food expenses! That would be amazing!

03:19.910 --> 03:23.260
But then we can no longer experience the joy of eating cake.

03:23.260 --> 03:24.850
You've got a point.

03:25.350 --> 03:30.730
Anyway, may "Operation: Get Squishy to Make our Names get Carried Down to Posterity" begin!

03:31.020 --> 03:31.660
Roger!

03:33.880 --> 03:35.670
How's this, Eievui? Does it feel nice?

03:37.350 --> 03:40.030
Eievui is slowly getting used to everyone.

03:40.030 --> 03:40.650
Yeah!

03:41.180 --> 03:42.780
This little one is a hard worker, after all.

03:46.910 --> 03:47.910
Done!

03:48.200 --> 03:49.120
Ta-da!

03:49.670 --> 03:52.890
Serena's special pochette-with-a-room-for-Squishy!

03:53.240 --> 03:54.680
Whoa! All right!

03:55.720 --> 03:57.000
Serena, thank you!

03:58.670 --> 03:59.910
Squishy, look, look!

04:03.850 --> 04:05.240
Now the problem's solved.

04:05.750 --> 04:07.270
Thank you very much, Serena.

04:07.500 --> 04:08.840
You're welcome.

04:09.350 --> 04:10.970
I hope it'll like it.

04:12.040 --> 04:14.310
Serena, it's saying that it likes it very much!

04:17.190 --> 04:18.150
Thank goodness.

04:19.610 --> 04:22.650
Come on, Eievui! Let's practice for the Tripokalon!

04:34.750 --> 04:36.230
Yeah, you're doing nicely!

04:50.090 --> 04:51.220
Eievui, are you all right?

04:52.310 --> 04:53.520
I've never seen this Pokémon before.

04:55.100 --> 04:58.950
Hariborg, the Spiny Armor Pokémon. The evolved form of Harimaron.

04:59.320 --> 05:01.670
The solid shell around its body is so sturdy it is able to withstand...

05:01.670 --> 05:04.190
...the impact of even something the size of a tractor-trailer truck without flinching.

05:04.680 --> 05:09.500
This shell repels attacks while it strikes with its pointed spines.

05:12.120 --> 05:13.740
The evolved form of Harimaron...

05:21.050 --> 05:23.110
Its Vine Whip has the shape of a heart!

05:23.370 --> 05:26.060
Does that mean Hariborg is in love with Eievui?

05:26.550 --> 05:28.050
What? Love at first sight?

05:34.350 --> 05:35.640
This time it is Rollout!

05:36.060 --> 05:37.020
What are you gonna do, Serena?

05:37.350 --> 05:38.440
What do you mean, "What are you gonna do?"

05:38.760 --> 05:40.920
I can hardly tell it that it should stop liking it...

05:46.810 --> 05:47.710
Yancham!

05:47.710 --> 05:48.320
Harimaron!

06:17.830 --> 06:20.230
What's with that guy? So noisy...

06:20.810 --> 06:22.140
Is the battle over already?

06:22.780 --> 06:25.550
I cannot believe it went down even though it was not even a damaging move.

06:26.140 --> 06:28.890
Anyway, thank goodness Eievui was not hurt.

06:33.830 --> 06:34.520
Eievui?

06:46.380 --> 06:47.930
Oh, it woke up.

06:48.220 --> 06:48.890
Are you all right?

06:50.860 --> 06:52.140
Oh, thanks.

06:52.350 --> 06:54.300
It is surprisingly polite.

06:56.300 --> 06:56.470
Huh?

06:57.270 --> 06:57.990
There it goes.

06:58.830 --> 07:00.200
Maybe it's given up already?

07:02.310 --> 07:03.400
Oh, here it comes again.

07:04.700 --> 07:06.630
This time it's the gift tactic...

07:06.970 --> 07:08.250
I see.

07:14.460 --> 07:15.850
Maybe it's not its type?

07:16.150 --> 07:21.960
Hm... I want Eievui to meet and become friends with lots of different Pokémon, but...

07:32.310 --> 07:33.740
Oh geez!

07:34.170 --> 07:35.950
Stop fighting already.

07:36.280 --> 07:38.440
It does not look like it is working.

07:38.710 --> 07:41.480
Roughnecks are even less popular with girls, just so you know.

08:01.960 --> 08:03.100
What's up this time?

08:03.290 --> 08:05.470
I wonder if it wants to battle Yancham.

08:05.750 --> 08:07.040
So it regained its motivation!

08:07.690 --> 08:08.590
What's this about?

08:08.920 --> 08:13.110
Maybe it wants to show Eievui its strength by battling Yancham.

08:13.400 --> 08:15.550
I see! It wants to show off its good side.

08:15.830 --> 08:20.350
I wonder if that'll work. I have a feeling this is not the kind of thing Eievui likes...

08:23.470 --> 08:24.730
What are you gonna do, Yancham?

08:38.030 --> 08:42.040
Uh... Eievui seems to feel safe when it's with Horubee.

08:45.480 --> 08:46.730
Both of you, do your best!

08:56.810 --> 08:57.900
Yancham, dodge!

08:59.470 --> 09:00.430
Stone Edge!

09:10.090 --> 09:10.440
Evade it!

09:15.290 --> 09:15.910
Dark Pulse!

09:24.310 --> 09:24.760
It endured it!

09:25.100 --> 09:27.040
It reflexively blocked it with Needle Arm.

09:27.340 --> 09:27.750
Arm Thrust!

09:30.590 --> 09:31.880
Yancham, are you all right?

09:41.430 --> 09:43.430
What? Now you want to fight Harimaron?

09:52.570 --> 09:54.030
Harimaron, do your best!

10:02.730 --> 10:03.200
Dodge!

10:05.100 --> 10:05.960
Tackle!

10:12.110 --> 10:14.380
It's more nimble than it looks.

10:15.980 --> 10:16.670
Pin Missile!

10:26.550 --> 10:27.270
That didn't do much...

10:28.040 --> 10:29.370
I can't believe how hard its body is.

10:30.730 --> 10:31.450
Maintain a distance!

11:19.150 --> 11:19.670
Eievui!

11:20.010 --> 11:21.290
Squishy! Dedenne!

11:21.290 --> 11:21.740
Horubee!

11:21.990 --> 11:23.270
Just what's going on?!

11:23.950 --> 11:25.780
If you ask us "What's going on?!",

11:26.200 --> 11:28.290
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

11:28.680 --> 11:30.790
We want to name the new Pokémon!

11:31.340 --> 11:33.400
We want to make our names get carried down!

11:33.740 --> 11:36.360
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

11:36.830 --> 11:39.300
we're lovely, charmy godparents!

11:40.150 --> 11:40.840
Musashi!

11:41.420 --> 11:41.840
Kojiro!

11:42.390 --> 11:45.270
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

11:45.480 --> 11:48.140
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

11:48.250 --> 11:49.750
Just kidding!

11:52.250 --> 11:53.200
Rocket Gang!

11:53.880 --> 11:55.980
Our "Operation: Fake Squishy" was a huge success!

11:56.270 --> 11:58.760
These Pokémon belong to us now.

11:58.760 --> 11:59.960
We got a huge haul!

11:59.960 --> 12:00.640
Bye!

12:00.990 --> 12:01.580
Wait!

12:07.910 --> 12:08.740
Fiarrow! Onbat!

12:12.120 --> 12:15.630
Please look for the Rocket Gang's balloon! It can't have gone that far.

12:25.710 --> 12:26.550
What are you doing?!

12:28.590 --> 12:29.670
Let's go search too.

12:29.930 --> 12:30.570
Yes.

12:37.070 --> 12:38.230
Pokémon Quiz!

12:39.020 --> 12:40.050
The answer is...?

13:30.430 --> 13:33.370
All right, what name should I pick...?

13:33.370 --> 13:35.880
I caught it, so I should name it.

13:35.880 --> 13:39.020
What are you talking about? What you get credit for I get credit for!

13:39.020 --> 13:41.000
Which means the Rocket Gang gets credit for it as well.

13:41.000 --> 13:42.090
Wrooong!

13:42.090 --> 13:43.900
Right, Musashi Beauty?

13:44.150 --> 13:44.880
Uh... Huh?!

13:47.450 --> 13:48.070
Oh no.

13:48.590 --> 13:49.640
It got away.

13:49.640 --> 13:50.830
Nyarth, turn back!

13:50.830 --> 13:51.820
Understood!

13:52.700 --> 13:54.460
We'll bring it back for sure!

13:54.730 --> 13:56.810
Musashi Beauty-chan!

14:00.750 --> 14:01.230
Did you find them?

14:03.270 --> 14:04.350
Please search for them some more!

14:17.390 --> 14:19.340
Hey, don't fight!

14:19.340 --> 14:20.110
Harimaron!

14:20.350 --> 14:21.590
Yancham, stop it!

14:21.980 --> 14:23.500
This isn't the time for quarreling.

14:26.060 --> 14:28.930
You've got to work together if you want to help your friends!

14:36.140 --> 14:37.670
How dare you escape?

14:37.960 --> 14:40.190
Come on, hand that thing over.

14:44.440 --> 14:46.440
Go, Pumpjin!

14:46.440 --> 14:48.070
Come out, Maaiika!

14:56.940 --> 14:57.580
Tackle!

15:05.150 --> 15:07.260
Go, Shadow Ball!

15:20.460 --> 15:21.350
Dark Pulse!

15:25.990 --> 15:27.440
Follow it up with Seed Bomb!

15:38.090 --> 15:40.250
All right, the obstacles are gone.

15:40.760 --> 15:43.420
Come over here, Musashi Beauty.

15:43.420 --> 15:44.920
It's "Toe Beans Nyarth"!

15:45.130 --> 15:46.380
"Great Kojiro"!

15:46.540 --> 15:48.870
But that sounds like the name of a pro wrestler!

15:48.870 --> 15:54.870
Anyway, if we send this guy to Sakaki-sama our reputation will go through the roof, no doubt!

15:56.700 --> 15:57.320
Those guys...!

15:57.990 --> 15:58.830
We've found you!

16:00.230 --> 16:01.870
I knew it was the brats!

16:01.870 --> 16:02.770
You're so pesky!

16:04.600 --> 16:06.120
Squishy! Dedenne!

16:06.120 --> 16:07.750
Eievui, are you all right?

16:07.960 --> 16:09.150
Horubee, well done.

16:09.510 --> 16:11.440
We won't let you get away any more, Rocket Gang!

16:17.030 --> 16:18.190
Oh geez...

16:26.060 --> 16:28.950
You've got to work together if you want to help your friends!

16:34.360 --> 16:35.470
What's with those guys?

16:36.040 --> 16:40.760
It's saying, "Let's make a truce for now. If we don't support each other we won't be able to help our friends."

16:41.110 --> 16:42.220
What's this about?

16:47.240 --> 16:47.980
Guys...

16:50.990 --> 16:53.450
What? You guys wanna fight?

16:53.930 --> 16:55.710
Use Psybeam, Maaiika!

17:06.670 --> 17:07.710
So cheeky...!

17:08.040 --> 17:09.550
Maaiika, Tackle!

17:16.410 --> 17:17.080
Geez...

17:17.320 --> 17:18.720
Pumpjin, Seed Bomb!

17:25.660 --> 17:26.770
They're really something!

17:52.950 --> 17:55.390
This feels bad!

17:59.670 --> 18:01.150
See you!

18:01.850 --> 18:04.470
You guys make a good team.

18:04.910 --> 18:06.060
See, you can do it if you try!

18:18.410 --> 18:19.560
Uh, Hariborg?

18:24.650 --> 18:25.750
Oh, there it is again.

18:40.620 --> 18:42.070
Hariborg, I'm sorry.

18:42.590 --> 18:46.030
I don't think Eievui <i>dislikes</i> you, but...

18:46.630 --> 18:50.170
It's shy with strangers and has a hard time coming out of its shell.

19:04.940 --> 19:06.810
I'm glad they've become friends!

19:06.810 --> 19:09.230
Though its love did not bear fruit...

19:32.940 --> 19:34.620
It recovers fast.

19:35.240 --> 19:36.870
We worried over nothing.

19:37.690 --> 19:40.110
All right, let's go back to practicing for the Tripokalon.

19:43.370 --> 19:45.990
All right. Pikachu, we're going to train!

19:48.510 --> 19:51.260
Well then, let us prepare lunch, shall we?

19:51.690 --> 19:53.290
Yeah, I'm hungry!

19:54.120 --> 19:55.720
What should I do?

19:55.910 --> 19:57.740
Eureka, can you fetch some water for me?

19:57.740 --> 19:58.070
Yeah!

20:00.310 --> 20:02.460
With meetings come partings.

20:03.530 --> 20:09.990
Watching Hariborg moving on to a new love, Satoshi and his friends continue their journey.

20:16.040 --> 20:21.010
Sunday November 8th at 8am!

20:16.550 --> 20:18.700
There is a huge gathering of Pokénds at Pokénchi!

20:18.220 --> 20:20.570
You're getting too engrossed in Pokémon!

20:19.020 --> 20:20.570
On Sunday at 8am!

20:23.800 --> 20:25.740
PokéLove TV!

20:26.270 --> 20:30.840
All right, here comes PokéLove TV, which spreads the charm of Pokémon to the world!

20:30.840 --> 20:32.490
The hosts are me, Ken, and...

20:32.490 --> 20:34.640
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:34.840 --> 20:38.990
Jenny, today we're introducing the Evolution Pokémon Eievui; do you know about it?

20:39.160 --> 20:42.590
"Evolution Pokémon"? Other Pokémon evolve too, so why...?

20:42.590 --> 20:46.630
Jenny, Eievui's evolutions aren't comparable to those of other Pokémon!

20:46.630 --> 20:50.440
You won't believe it, but at the moment, eight evolutions have been discovered!

20:50.440 --> 20:52.300
What? Eight?!

20:52.300 --> 20:55.480
Yeah... It makes it hard to decide which one to evolve it into...

20:55.720 --> 20:56.680
I've decided.

20:56.680 --> 20:58.330
What? Which one will you pick?

20:58.330 --> 21:00.650
I'll catch lots of them and evolve them into every one of those!

21:01.130 --> 21:02.300
Wait for me, you all!

21:03.320 --> 21:06.670
Come to think of it, Hariborg fell in love with a Booster at first sight.

21:06.990 --> 21:10.950
But Booster is a Fire type, so I wonder if they're even compatible...

21:18.300 --> 21:20.140
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.330 --> 21:21.510
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.590 --> 21:28.950
The Joy-san we meet on our way often leaves the Pokémon Center unattended due to getting caught up in searching for Mega Stones.

21:28.950 --> 21:30.490
Oops! I'll open it now!

21:30.710 --> 21:31.670
Uh... Huh?!

21:32.440 --> 21:33.320
Does it not open?

21:33.320 --> 21:34.680
Don't tell me... Tabunne...!

21:35.150 --> 21:35.950
"Tabunne"?

21:36.590 --> 21:39.270
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:39.590 --> 21:42.520
Mega Tabunne VS Giga Giga Nyarth!!

21:42.560 --> 21:46.010
Next Time

21:42.560 --> 21:46.010
Mega Tabunne VS Giga Giga Nyarth!!

21:43.020 --> 21:44.950
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:46.050 --> 21:56.060
Next episode:

21:46.050 --> 21:51.020
The group meets a slightly eccentric Joy!

21:46.910 --> 21:51.480
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

21:51.080 --> 21:56.060
Tabunne mega evolves!?
